Subject: Carry the Fil-C QuickJS port forward to 2026-06-04
Origin: Filnix, adapted from ports/patch/quickjs.patch (upstream Fil-C, 2024-02-14)
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

The same three changes as upstream Fil-C's port of the 2024-02-14 snapshot:
no computed-goto dispatch; keep the autoinit realm pointer in a pointer (the
realm is recovered by pointer arithmetic, so it keeps its capability); and
use qsort_r instead of rqsort, whose exchange helpers copy pointers as
integer words. The 2024 greedy-regexp fix is not needed: libregexp's
matcher was rewritten and keeps positions in a pointer union.
tests/quickjs-regexp.js runs in the port's install check.

Workers also need to recover SAB backing pointers from their existing live
pointer table, not from serialized integers. JS_ReadObject2 borrows that
table and matches serialized addresses without reconstructing capabilities.
The constructor still takes a reference before the message releases its
queue reference; serialization bytes and JS object-reference semantics are
unchanged. Byte-only SAB reads fail explicitly under Fil-C; native builds
retain the legacy API. Free the writer's pointer table on failed writes or
when no caller requests it. Worker sharing and reader lifetime regressions
run alongside the upstream make test suite.

